<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rhodri Molwynog</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 754</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Rhodri Molwynog ap Idwal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rhodri Molwynog was a king of Gwynedd in the first half of the eighth century, whose death the Welsh annals record in 754. He belonged to the royal line descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cadwallon-ap-cadfan">Cadwallon ap Cadfan</a>. His sons Cynan Dindaethwy and Hywel later fought each other for the kingdom, and after Hywel's death in 825 the throne passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merfyn-frych">Merfyn Frych</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rhodri-molwynog.jpg" alt="Rhodri Molwynog" width="320" height="308" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Powell and Humphrey Lloyd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rhodrimolwynog_historieofcambria.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
